  "body": "Bloct 2.0.0 introduces continuous, source-preserving block editing.\n\n- Click document text to edit at the clicked position; press Escape to return to reading while preserving the draft, Undo history and scroll position. Save explicitly with Command-S.\n- Edit paragraphs, headings, lists, tasks, code, equations, images and simple GFM tables in one editor. Markdown typing rules and a trailing Text line support continuous input.\n- Navigate tables with arrow keys, Enter, Tab and Shift-Enter; select equations with the keyboard and open their editor with Enter or Space.\n- Share the same offline math renderer, fonts and document appearance across reading and editing. Unsupported syntax stays in protected source nodes.\n\nRequires macOS 14 or later. The ZIP contains Apple Silicon and Intel binaries built with macOS SDK 27.\n\nValidation: model, native save/state, WebKit appearance/click/input, hosted and relative-image regressions passed. Public ZIP version, checksum and source resources were verified. [Validation evidence](https://github.com/JAEHYEON-BAE/bloct/blob/v2.0.0/Tests/results/2026-11-10/release-2.0.0-checks.json).\n\nKnown limitations: a native window-close crash remains under investigation ([bug 45](https://github.com/JAEHYEON-BAE/bloct/blob/v2.0.0/BUG_FIXES.md#bug-45)). Real Korean IME, first-save/conflict panels, rich clipboard/PDF, advanced table/image controls, performance and public Release GUI acceptance remain partially or wholly unverified; see [F5](https://github.com/JAEHYEON-BAE/bloct/blob/v2.0.0/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md#f5-notion-\ubc29\uc2dd\uc758-\ube14\ub85d-\uad00\ub9ac\uc640-\uc5f0\uc18d-\ud3b8\uc9d1).\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/JAEHYEON-BAE/bloct/compare/v1.8.0...v2.0.0\n"
